    count: 1
    covers: "BodyViewer.test.tsx (+1 test, +1 extended): the switch renders radios named pretty (checked on open) and raw, and NO radio named decoded - the absence is the assertion that catches a half-done rename, which is the only failure mode a rename has. The existing raw-segment test keeps its behavioural claim (refetch with false, dispatch on bytes) and gains the return trip: clicking pretty refetches with true and the type-dispatched renderer comes back. Both were verified RED first (no radio named pretty existed). SegmentedControl.test.tsx: fixture renamed to the sighting it models, positions kept because the roving-tabindex tests index into it. Seven of the eight tests carry the renamed option name inside their queries, since each query addresses an option by accessible name; the one test that names no option is byte-identical. Green before and after with no matcher, subject or count changed - which is the plan's check in the form that can be met. The plan asked for every assertion 'green UNEDITED', which no fixture rename can satisfy, and rounds 3, 5 and 7 each caught a copy of that false claim - twice in the result report and once here, in this note. api.test.ts: a local name only; both query-string assertions (true -> ?decode=1, false -> ?decode=source) untouched over the renamed parameter, and they are the guard that renaming the boolean moved no wire behaviour."
  integration:
    count: 1
    covers: "ui/src/App.test.tsx - the bounded contract is the switch inside the mounted shell over a scripted TrawlerApi. One test (retitled and extended, RED first): opening a flow's response leg renders the switch with both new names, asserts no radio named decoded survives, and pins getBody(id, 'response', true) with the type-dispatched render - the label and the fetch together, because a switch reading 'pretty' over a source fetch would satisfy either assertion alone."
  e2e:
    count: 1
    covers: "ui/e2e/specs/flows.spec.ts UC-5, against the real WebKit window and an ephemeral core - the assertion the epic plan assigns to W9. The existing toggle spec is renamed and extended rather than duplicated: the switch's two segments exist by exact label, no segment named decoded exists, then the toggle walk it already performed still finds minified source text one way and indented JSON the other. The compressed-body raw spec drives the same renamed helper, so the rename is proven over two body kinds. 32 passing; onboarding.spec.ts UNEDITED and green, this epic's standing check that the re-design left."
